(* groups-removal.pv - membership change (8.3): the attacker holds D, a member
   of epoch 0 removed in epoch 1. Epoch 1 stays secret from D, and no member
   but D itself accepts anything from D in epoch 1. (D still computes its
   pairwise MACs; it is the attested roster that refuses its sender key. D can
   fool its own client - it knows its own rk_D - which deceives nobody.) *)
query attacker(secret1).
query m: bitstring, x: G; event(Accept(x, exp(g, ikD), m, e1)) ==> event(Corrupt(x)).
process Group(false, true) | Hand(ikD)
